## Library layer

**`/output/lib/pytypes/unicodedata.mjs`** — Unicode character classes for `int()`/`strip()`
```js
// Unicode helpers needed to mimic `str.strip()` and `int()` character classes.

// Characters Python treats as whitespace when parsing a numeric literal.  This
// is the Unicode White_Space property: it includes NEL (U+0085), NBSP and the
// space separators, but *not* U+200B or the BOM, and not the C0 separators
// U+001C..U+001F.
const WHITESPACE = new Set(
  [0x09, 0x0a, 0x0b, 0x0c, 0x0d, 0x20, 0x85, 0xa0, 0x1680, 0x2028, 0x2029, 0x202f, 0x205f, 0x3000]
    .concat(Array.from({ length: 11 }, (_, i) => 0x2000 + i)) // U+2000..U+200A
);
```
Plus `pyStrip`, `isDecimalDigit`, and `decimalDigitValue` — the last walks back to the start of the surrounding run of `\p{Nd}` characters and takes the offset mod 10, so `int('٣')` and `int('١٢٣')` work like Python's even in the adjacent mathematical-digit blocks.

**`/output/lib/pytypes/pyint.mjs`** — `int(text)` returning `BigInt` (arbitrary precision, sign, `_` separators only between digits, `-0` → `0`).
**`/output/lib/pytypes/repr.mjs`** — `repr()`/`str()`: `True`/`False`, list, tuple (with 1-tuple comma), Python string escaping.
**`/output/lib/pytypes/containers.mjs`** — `PyTuple`, and `PyDict` keeping insertion order with Python's `True == 1` key equivalence.
**`/output/lib/errors/pyerrors.mjs`** + **`linecache.mjs`** — exception classes and the CPython traceback, including the fact that the source line and `^^^^^^` anchors appear only when `test7.py` is reachable from the cwd.
**`/output/lib/io/stdio.mjs`** + **`print.mjs`** — `writeSync`-based output so `process.exit` can't truncate, and `pyPrint`.
**`/output/lib/iterutils/`** — `keyfunc.mjs` (Python truthiness, callable-or-attribute keys), `partition.mjs` → `(trues, falses)`, `bucketize.mjs` → ordered dict of lists with optional `valueTransform`/`keyFilter`, re-exported by `index.mjs`.
**`/output/lib/argparse/`** — `actions.mjs`, `textwrap.mjs` (greedy wrap that breaks on hyphens), `formatter.mjs` (usage-part regex, the width-clamped help column), `parser.mjs` (negative-number classification, `=` form, abbreviations, clustered short flags, `--`, required-before-unrecognized ordering), `index.mjs`.

